## Apply task progress overlay to Batch Auto-Map page

Context: The ontology wizard now shows a branded spinner with step checklist and
activity log during async work. The Batch Auto-Map page still used a minimal inline
progress bar with only the latest message. This reuses the same overlay pattern so
users can follow auto-map agent steps live.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/global/js/task-progress-ui.js
   Extract shared overlay builder, step checklist, activity log, and agent-steps
   panel used by wizard and auto-map.
2. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-wizard.js
   Delegate to `TaskProgressUI` instead of inline render helpers.
3. src/front/static/mapping/js/mapping-autoassign.js
   Full-page overlay on `#autoassign-section` with step log + activity trace;
   live gauge updates preserved during polling.
4. src/front/templates/partials/mapping/_mapping_autoassign.html
   Remove legacy inline progress card (overlay is JS-driven).
5. src/front/templates/mapping.html, src/front/templates/ontology.html
   Load `task-progress-ui.js` before wizard/auto-map modules.
6. src/front/static/global/css/components.css
   Generalize overlay styles to `.task-progress-*` (wizard aliases kept).
7. src/api/routers/internal/mapping.py, src/back/objects/mapping/Mapping.py
   Align auto-map task steps with init → prepare → agent → finalize and advance
   through them during the background run.

