## Harden Unity Catalog SQL against identifier injection

Context: External PR #53 flagged f-string SQL in `UnityCatalog` (catalog/schema/table
from API query params). The finding was valid but the patch was stale and incomplete.
This adds centralized UC identifier validation, backtick-quoted FQNs, parameterized
literals where supported, coverage for newer probe methods, and restores the
`DatabricksAuth` CloudFetch recursion guard dropped in the #61 revert.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/uc_identifiers.py
   New module: validate/quote UC segments (`^[a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_-]*$`, reject `--`).
2. src/back/core/databricks/UnityCatalog.py
   Guard all warehouse SQL paths; parameterize `get_table_comment` and
   `probe_schema_has_tables` value clauses.
3. src/back/core/helpers/SQLHelpers.py
   Thin delegates to `uc_identifiers` for reuse elsewhere.
4. src/back/core/databricks/DatabricksAuth.py
   Restore `_resolving_cloud_fetch` guard from #29.
5. tests/units/core/test_unity_catalog.py
   Update SQL expectations; add injection, probe, and select-permission tests.
6. tests/units/core/test_uri_sql_helpers.py
   Cover UC identifier helpers via `SQLHelpers` delegates.

Modified files:
- src/back/core/uc_identifiers.py
- src/back/core/databricks/UnityCatalog.py
- src/back/core/helpers/SQLHelpers.py
- src/back/core/databricks/DatabricksAuth.py
- tests/units/core/test_unity_catalog.py
- tests/units/core/test_uri_sql_helpers.py

